{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The three artifacts this dispute turns on describe one and the same trip: TRIP_RECORD EV-TRIP-00113, GPS_TRACE EV-GPS-00113 and FARE_BREAKDOWN EV-FARE-00113 each carry trip_id TRP-00113, and the trace's first fix at 18:47:10 is the trip record's started_at. Limb (a) of POL-RD-08 is therefore satisfied on a single coherent record, and the trace itself is a 217-fix, 100%-coverage series at a 10-second interval with no gap at all — so nothing in this case is a measurement dispute. The disagreement is entirely about which baseline POL-RD-01 uses.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00113", "EV-GPS-00113", "EV-FARE-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is a RYDE_POOL booking, so POL-RD-12 fixes the baseline at the matched-itinerary optimal on trip_record.optimal_distance_km — 19.40 km, the Punggol -> Hougang co-rider pickup -> Raffles Place route the platform computed at match time, and which the SYSTEM notice MSG-00113-001 put in front of the rider at 18:42:04, read at 18:42:31, before the 18:47:10 start. The 15.8 km figure in the filed claim is solo_optimal_distance_km, which POL-RD-12 carries for reference only and which fails on that ground alone. The rider does not press it, and asks the tribunal to hold the platform to its own pooled figure of 19.40 km rather than to the 20.2 km it actually billed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00113", "EV-CHAT-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Measured as POL-RD-01 requires — gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 20.18 km against the 19.40 km matched-itinerary optimal — the excess is 0.78 km, or 4.02%. POL-RD-01 makes the establishment test conjunctive: the excess must be greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% of optimal, and 0.78 km fails the absolute limb. The rider therefore accepts, on this trip's distance figures, that no deviation is established and that POL-RD-02 has no trigger. The billed 20.2 km on the fare breakdown is the rounded convenience copy POL-RD-01 forbids citing for the threshold test, and even that figure is exactly 0.8 km — not greater than 0.8 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00113", "EV-TRIP-00113", "EV-FARE-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-12"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Should the tribunal nonetheless reach the money, the POL-RD-02 arithmetic runs on the platform's own pooled figure and is not discretionary: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 19.40 + 0.28 x 34.0) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP - 3.00 promo discount = a recomputed fare of 25.67 against a charged_total of 26.83. The difference is 1.16, rounded up to 1.20. That 1.16 is precisely the unmatched running the rider was billed for: the distance charge alone (0.75 x 20.2 = 15.15) is 0.60 above the 14.55 the matched itinerary supports, and the time charge (0.28 x 36.0 = 10.08) is 0.56 above the 9.52 the 34-minute quote supports. Any refund in this case is therefore 1.20 computed on 19.40 km, not the notional 6.00 in the claim text, and the ruling must state charged_total, recomputed_fare and the refund on separate lines.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00113", "EV-TRIP-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-12"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no external event on this record that can excuse the route, and the rider asks that the driver's account be tested on this trip's own numbers rather than on a cause no artifact supports. The TRAFFIC_ADVISORY artifact EV-ADVIS-00113-01 is MISSING — it has no payload, carries weight 0.0 and its issue code is MISSING_ARTIFACT — so no advisory names any road, expressway segment or junction on the Punggol, Hougang or CTE corridors in the 18:41-19:23 window, and the driver cannot bring himself within POL-RD-03. Nor is there any pass-through line that could be set against the rider the other way: erp_gantries is empty and tolls_erp is 0.00, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to operate on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00113-01", "EV-FARE-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own record adds no hurdle to this claim. On EV-RPROF-00113, rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0; the enhanced-corroboration condition in POL-RD-08 bites only where deviation_claims_60d is 4 or more AND deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 1 or fewer, so on a conjunctive test it cannot fire and the claim falls to be weighed on this trip's artifacts alone. No other field on either profile is relied on here, and under POL-GEN-01 none of them — rating, account_age_days, lifetime_trips, prior_deviation_flags or any like counter — may ground a finding for or against either party.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both sides are reading the same numbers, and the numbers decide this. This was a RYDE_POOL booking, so POL-RD-12 fixes the baseline at the MATCHED-ITINERARY optimal the platform computed at match time — 19.4 km on trip_record.optimal_distance_km, the Punggol -> Hougang co-rider pickup -> Raffles Place route — and not the 15.8 km solo_optimal_distance_km the filed claim used. That 15.8 km figure is carried for reference only, and a claim measured against it fails on that ground alone. Measured the way POL-RD-01 requires, gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 20.18 km (the 20.2 km on the fare breakdown is the rounded convenience copy POL-RD-01 forbids citing for the threshold test). Excess over the 19.4 km baseline is 0.78 km, or 4.02%. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is greater than 0.8 km absolute AND greater than 20% of optimal — both tests must pass. 0.78 km fails the absolute limb and 4.02% fails the percentage limb, and even the rounded 20.2 km billed figure gives exactly 0.8 km, which is still not greater than 0.8 km. No deviation is established, so POL-RD-02 never triggers: its recomputation is expressly conditional on 'where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01', and the rider's own arithmetic (recomputed_fare 25.67 against charged_total 26.83, a 1.16 difference rounded to 1.20) is therefore not reached. The Hougang leg the rider complains of is the platform-matched co-rider pickup, which POL-RD-12 excludes from excess in any event, and the rider was told of the pooled route and the 19.4 km / 34 min estimate in the SYSTEM message at 18:42:04, read at 18:42:31, before the trip started at 18:47:10. There is no billing-integrity correction either: erp_gantries is empty, tolls_erp is 0.00, no airport surcharge applies, and the billed distance (20.2 km) is not less than the traced distance (20.18 km), so nothing is owed the driver under POL-RD-04. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00113-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) but nothing turns on it: no exoneration clause needs to run, because the deviation test fails on the arithmetic before POL-RD-03 is reached. No profile field has been used to establish anything about this trip, and the profile mention is context only. Outcome: the contested charge of $26.83 (amount contested $6.00) stands, no refund issues and the driver is owed nothing. Confidence 0.95, resting on the GPS trace and the trip record, both at full weight 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
